# Step 1: Run the agent you have today

In this step you run Wanda exactly as the {{ s.lab.company }} support team runs it today, so you have a baseline and can see the gaps a buyer will find. Nothing here uses Databricks yet.

## 1.1 Look at the code

Open `step1-external-agent/` from the lab files.

| File | What it does |
|---|---|
| `wanda/agent.py` | Wanda's instructions and the OpenAI Agents SDK `Agent` |
| `wanda/tools.py` | Five tools: `get_booking`, `list_guest_bookings`, `quote_refund`, `get_refund_policy`, `issue_refund` |
| `wanda/policy.py` | The refund policy, with {{ f.today }} as "today" |
| `wanda/main.py` | Reads `MODEL_BASE_URL`, `MODEL_API_KEY` and `MODEL_NAME` from `.env`, then runs one question |
| `data/*.csv` | The snapshot the tools read: {{ f.snapshot_bookings }} bookings plus their guests, properties and payments |

The model client is the standard OpenAI client pointed at `MODEL_BASE_URL`. That one setting is why Step 2 needs no code change.

## 1.2 Run Wanda against your model provider

1. Open a terminal in `step1-external-agent/` and copy the settings file:

    ```bash
    cp .env.example .env
    ```

2. Put your provider key in `MODEL_API_KEY` in `.env`. Keep `MODEL_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1` and `MODEL_NAME=gpt-4.1-mini`.
3. Ask Wanda about a booking:

    ```bash
    uv run wanda "What is the status of booking 532?"
    ```

4. Verify that Wanda says booking 532 is **confirmed**, at a **{{ case[532].property }}**, checking in on **{{ case[532].check_in }}**.
5. Ask about a cancellation:

    ```bash
    uv run wanda "I want to cancel booking 166. How much would I get back?"
    ```

6. Verify the refund is **${{ case[166].refund }}**, a **{{ case[166].rule }}**, because check-in is {{ case[166].days }} days away.

!!! tip "No provider key?"
    Skip the runs in 1.2. In Step 2 you point the same code at Unity Gateway and run it there.

## 1.3 List the governance gaps

Look at what you just ran and note what a buyer's security review would find:

- **Model access:** one API key in a file. You cannot tell who called the model, limit usage per person, or see what was sent.
- **Data:** the CSV snapshot has no access control, no lineage back to the source and no record of who read which guest's data. It is already out of date.
- **Actions:** `issue_refund` runs as soon as the model calls it.
- **Records:** nothing is traced. If a guest complains, you cannot replay what happened.
- **Quality:** there is no test set and no definition of a good answer.

The rest of the lab closes these gaps in order.

